DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssyyssllooggdd utility reads and logs messages to the system console, log
     files, other machines and/or users as specified by its configuration
     file.

     The options are as follows:

     --44      Force ssyyssllooggdd to use IPv4 addresses only.

     --66      Force ssyyssllooggdd to use IPv6 addresses only.

     --88      Tells ssyyssllooggdd not to interfere with 8-bit data.  Normally ssyyssllooggdd
             will replace C1 control characters (ISO 8859 and Unicode
             characters) with their “M-_x” equivalent.  Note, this option does
             not change the way ssyyssllooggdd alters control characters (see
             iscntrl(3)).  They will always be replaced with their “^_x” equiv‐
             alent.

     --AA      Ordinarily, ssyyssllooggdd tries to send the message to only one address
             even if the host has more than one A or AAAA record.  If this op‐
             tion is specified, ssyyssllooggdd tries to send the message to all ad‐
             dresses.

